cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "format-bench: a benchmark for data-format conversion"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Al Yacoub
    given-names: Angelo
    email: angeloalyacoub1@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/hadestructhor/format-bench"
url: "https://hadestructhor.github.io/format-bench/"
abstract: >-
  format-bench measures whether a language model can convert data between
  serialization formats without corrupting it. 2,025 frozen test cases span nine
  directions (text, JSON, YAML, CSV to JSON, YAML, CSV), five structural depth
  levels, eight domains, and seven orthogonal transformation constraints (type
  coercion, unit stripping, enum normalisation, range clamping, escaping,
  wrapping, counting). Each case is graded on two axes: task (the correct value
  appears anywhere in the reply) and strict (the whole reply is exactly the
  value). Every model is measured twice, with and without a worked example.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - structured output
  - JSON
  - YAML
  - CSV
  - data transformation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-24
